Laboratory competence — ISO/IEC 17025 and open technical guidance (@met-competence: 0, is #reference, #part-of @met-sources) { r_0RT4JM2Q799A0FYNA35H1Q8Y2Z
ISO/IEC 17025:2017. General requirements for the competence of testing and calibration laboratories, third edition, corrected 2018-03. [Official publisher’s description and preview](https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html).

The full ISO text is copyrighted and ordinarily sold or accessed through an institutional subscription. It is a professional reference for a real laboratory’s applicable requirements; it is not represented here as an open book or reproduced standard. The free catalogue description and preview identify its scope. The publisher page inspected on 28 October 2026 stated that the edition remained current after confirmation in 2023.

For the trail’s required technical work use the freely readable NIST traceability, measurement-process, and uncertainty sources and the Eurachem validation guide. Compare them with the full standard where authorized access exists. Distinguish technical competence, accreditation for a particular scope, metrological traceability of a result, and a product’s conformity.

Retain the publisher’s rights and the actual edition in any reference. No purchase, registration, or unauthorized copy is required to follow the open learning progression.

**Return:** [Measurement and metrology sources — books, guides, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_6H584EJ2Z9D11PG89Y21Y8T1A3).
